{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Having Second Thoughts"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Wish I Had"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le11ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional - Talking Hypothetically About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you hadn't come that night you couldn't have rescued me from that horribly hostile customer who nearly beat up my sous chef!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I hadn't gone to that party at your restaurant, I wouldn't have met Amy."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If she had really cared for me, she shouldn't have done that."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I hadn't spilled wine on his shoe, he wouldn't have been distracted at the right moment."}, {"type": "example", "content": " He wouldn't have slipped and broken his ankle which rendered him helpless for the rest of the night. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He also would have beaten up Pascal. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If none of that had happened, then the ambulance wouldn't have come and Amy wouldn't have entered my life."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could have</span> (+ past participle) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>something was possible in the past, or you had the ability to do something in the past, but you didn't do it</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you hadn't come that night you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">couldn't have rescued</span> me from that horribly hostile customer who nearly beat up my sous chef! \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Should have</span> (+ past participle) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>something would have been a good idea, but you didn't do it.</li></ul> </li><li> use it to give advice about the past when you say it to someone else, or to express regret about what you did or didn't do when you're talking about yourself</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If she had really cared for me, she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">shouldn't have done</span> that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> ( + past participle)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</li><li>talk about something you wanted to do but didn't</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I hadn't gone to that party at your restaurant, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wouldn't have met</span> Amy. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the third conditional is: <br> <span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\"italic\">could/should/would (not) have</span> + past participle"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking about Wishes"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, plus the past form of the verb or the past participle of the verb to talk about imaginary situations in the past, present or future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Wishes and sentences in the second and third conditional infer that what you want is probably not possible, or for some reason impossible and that you regret what happened in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I also wish you would change the subject. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "  I wish I could be more open. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I hadn't left my phone at work."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I didn't have to go back to work to get my phone."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Stucture\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">wish</span> + Simple Past</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk about wishes in the present or future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Sometimes I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wish I could be</span>more open.</span><br/> (I can't be more open.)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"underline\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">wish</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">had</span> + past participle</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk about wishes about past situations\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wish I hadn't left</span> my phone at work!</span><br/> (I left my phone at work.)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about a wish in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about a hypothetical situation in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about a wish in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about a hypothetical situation in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my paragraph with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tell a partner about a mistake you made in the past. (use wish)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner what you could have, should have done differently to avoid the mistake."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph of 100-120 words or more describing the mistake and what you could have done differently."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph to your partner."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to brood"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to keep thinking about something that you are worried or upset about"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why are you brooding Peter?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about emotions and behavior."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reticent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unwilling to talk about what you feel or what you know "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You've been so reticent recently."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hostile"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having or showing unfriendly feelings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You couldn't have rescued me from that horribly hostile customer who nearly beat up my sous chef."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to distract"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take someone's attention away from something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He wouldn't have been distracted at the right moment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to render"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to cause someone or something to be in a specific condition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He wouldn't have slipped and broken his ankle which rendered him helpless for the rest of the night."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lame"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "weak and unimpressive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She gave me some lame apology."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to have a wall up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to  establish a barrier in a relationship "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You really have a wall up."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "closed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not willing to accept new ideas or influences "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Why are you so closed?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le11ob02aud08"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions, behavior and work. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I wish for in the past, present or future."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Would your life have been better if you had been born in a different place? Explain."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " If you hadn't studied English what other language would you have chosen?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group